&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to an Engineering Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and work across team boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with PM, UX, legal, operations, or other non-engineering roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and take ownership to drive efforts to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and align the teams technical roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the best engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience working with backend tech (e.g. C++, Spanner)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience with Front End (Angular, Javascript, React, etc)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with 3rd party integrations and public APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TL or leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in product development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Google infrastructure (e.g. Flume, Borg, Protocol Buffers, OnePlatform) or GCP equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development experience with C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of frontend frameworks (e.g. Angular, Dart)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scalability experience&lt;/li&gt;
